# runtime user data lives under ~/.claude/oriel/, never in the repo
*.bak

# The private working repository, and everything that belongs to it: tickets, specs,
# research, agent skills, the agent-workflow docs and the project instructions that
# point at them. It describes the working process, not Oriel.
#
# It shares this directory rather than a second checkout of the same code, and it is
# its own git repository with its own private remote — so `git status` here can never
# see it, and there is no copy step between a working tree and a published one to get
# wrong (ADR 0012, amended). tests/CleanRoom.Tests.ps1 is what enforces this: an
# ignore rule that stops matching is silent, and the whole clean-room property rests
# on these five lines.
.workspace/
.scratch/
.agents/
.claude/
/CLAUDE.md

# .NET build output (ADR 0008: the widget is now a compiled Avalonia app)
bin/
obj/
dist/
